MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Blink doorbell feels like a useful next purchase because it adds visitor monitoring to my Alexa setup and connects with my earlier interest in door and window security.",
    "The memory card fits my history of storage and computer accessories, provided I have a compatible device that needs more space."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Older Echo Dots, Show 5 displays and Fire TV sticks repeat functions covered by my recent purchases, so their familiarity does not give me a reason to buy them now.",
    "The Ring charging station serves equipment I have not indicated owning, so it lacks a practical connection to my current setup."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Alexa purchases seem to be treated as interest in any Alexa device, even when it duplicates something I just bought.",
    "Interest in connected home devices seems to extend too readily to accessories that require specific equipment I may not own."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent device generations and Show 5 stand purchase suggest I am equipping and using my current devices, which makes older replacements less appealing.",
    "A related item needs to solve an additional problem: I would consider the doorbell first, while a larger display, car device or three-camera kit needs a clearer immediate purpose."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in Alexa and practical electronics but miss the difference between extending my setup and duplicating recent purchases."
}
